! OSPF - multi-area design with summarization (scales past flat area 0)
!
! Area layout: area 0 backbone, area 10 (user VLANs), area 20 (data center)
! ABR (R2) summarizes between areas so the core only sees aggregate routes.
!
router ospf 1
 router-id 2.2.2.2
 ! One area per set of interfaces instead of a flat single area
 network 10.0.0.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
 network 172.16.10.0 0.0.0.255 area 10
 network 172.16.20.0 0.0.0.255 area 20
 ! Loopback as stable router-id / iBGP source
 network 2.2.2.2 0.0.0.0 area 0

 ! Area 10 is a normal area; make area 20 a stub so no external
 ! LSAs cross it (default route injected instead)
 area 20 stub

 ! Summarize both stub/leaf areas on the ABR to the backbone
 area 10 range 172.16.10.0 255.255.254.0
 area 20 range 172.16.20.0 255.255.252.0

 passive-interface default
 no passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 no passive-interface GigabitEthernet0/1

 ! Only the ABR injects the default route
 default-information originate always

 ! Auth on the backbone segment so a rogue adjacency cannot form
 area 0 authentication message-digest
 interface GigabitEthernet0/0
  ip ospf message-digest-key 1 md5 BackboneKey01
  ip ospf authentication message-digest

 ! Tune timers for faster failure detection on the core uplink
 interface GigabitEthernet0/0
  ip ospf hello-interval 5
  ip ospf dead-interval 20
  ip ospf cost 10

! Verify
! show ip ospf neighbor
! show ip ospf database summary
! show ip route ospf
! show ip ospf interface brief
